{{Information
|description={{en|1=A smiling member of the ''[[:en:Ramnami Samaj|Ramnami Samaj]]'' sect.<br>This picture tells the story of a rebel community from [[:en:Chhattisgarh|Chhattisgarh]], India, called ''Ramnami Samaj''. They were fighting against the odds imposed on them by the society. These people used to belong to the lower caste, therefore they were forbidden to enter temples and to practice their religion. Being dominated by the Brahminical attitude, they started a silent non-violent revolt by tattooing राम, the name of [[:en:Rama|Lord Rama]], on their whole body and writing it on their clothes.}}
{{es|1=Miembro sonriente de la secta Rāmnāmī Samāj. Los seguidores de esta secta [[:es:Hinduismo|hindú]] rinden culto al dios [[:es:Rama (dios)|Rama]].}}
